          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The function <span class=\"math\">[MATH: g]</span> is defined by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: g(x) = 9x - 3.]</span> What is the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: g(-2)?]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "The function [MATH: g] is defined by [MATH: g(x) = 9x - 3.] What is the value of [MATH: g(-2)?]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To find <span class=\"math\">[MATH: g(-2),]</span> we substitute <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x = -2]</span> into the function definition and then simplify:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: g(x)|= 9x \u2212 3; g(\u2212 2)|= 9(\u2212 2) \u2212 3; = \u2212 18 \u2212 3; = \u2212 21]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To find [MATH: g(-2),] we substitute [MATH: x = -2] into the function definition and then simplify:\n[MATH: g(x)|= 9x \u2212 3; g(\u2212 2)|= 9(\u2212 2) \u2212 3; = \u2212 18 \u2212 3; = \u2212 21]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
