          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we calculate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: p(2).]</span> To do this, we substitute <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x = 2]</span> into the function definition <span class=\"math\">[MATH: p(x)]</span> and then simplify:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: p(x)|= x \u2212 1; p(2)|= 2 \u2212 1; = 1]</span></p><p>Next, we calculate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: q(2).]</span> To do this, we substitute <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x = 2]</span> into the function definition <span class=\"math\">[MATH: q(x)]</span> and then simplify:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: q(x)|= 3x; q(2)|= 3(2); = 6]</span></p><p>Now, we calculate <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4p(2) - q(2)]</span> as follows:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4p(2) \u2212 q(2)|= 4(1) \u2212 6; = 4 \u2212 6; = \u2212 2]</span></p>",
