    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nThis topic provides practice in evaluating linear functions for specific inputs and combining their values.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Evaluating a Function\n\nExample Prompt:\nThe function [MATH: g] is defined by [MATH: g(x) = 9x - 3.] What is the value of [MATH: g(-2)?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo find [MATH: g(-2),] we substitute [MATH: x = -2] into the function definition and then simplify:\n[MATH: g(x)|= 9x \u2212 3; g(\u2212 2)|= 9(\u2212 2) \u2212 3; = \u2212 18 \u2212 3; = \u2212 21]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nThe function [MATH: g] is defined by [MATH: g(x) = 50 \u2212 4x.] What is the value of [MATH: g(6)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 276]\nb. [MATH: 26]\nc. [MATH: 124]\nd. [MATH: 14]\ne. [MATH: 34]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nThe function [MATH: f] is defined by [MATH: f(x) = x + 75.] What is the value of [MATH: f(120)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 275]\nb. [MATH: 195]\nc. [MATH: 205]\nd. [MATH: 9, 000]\ne. [MATH: 185]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Evaluating a Function Containing Fractions\n\nExample Prompt:\nThe function [MATH: f] is defined by [MATH: f(x) = \\dfrac{5}{9}(x - 4).] What is the value of [MATH: f(22)?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo find [MATH: f(22),] we substitute [MATH: x = 22] into the function definition and then simplify:\n[MATH: f(x)|= (5)/(9)(x \u2212 4); f(22)|= (5)/(9)(22 \u2212 4); = (5)/(9)(18); = 10]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nThe function [MATH: g] is defined by [MATH: g(x) = x + (5)/(7).] What is the value of [MATH: g] when [MATH: x = (2)/(7)?][MATH: g((2)/(7)) =]\n[FREE_ENTRY 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: g] is the function defined by [MATH: g(x) = (4x + 3)/(5),] what is the value of [MATH: g(2)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 3]\nb. [MATH: 9]\nc. [MATH: 5]\nd. [MATH: (11)/(5)]\ne. [MATH: (7)/(5)]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Determining a Difference of Two Outputs\n\nExample Prompt:\nThe function [MATH: h] is defined by\n[MATH: h(x) = \\dfrac{x + 6}{6}.]\nWhat is the value of [MATH: h(6) - h(-6)?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we calculate [MATH: h(6).] To do this, we substitute [MATH: x = 6] into the function definition and then simplify:\n[MATH: h(x)|= (x + 6)/(6); h(6)|= (6 + 6)/(6); = (12)/(6); = 2]\n\nNext, we calculate [MATH: h(-6).] To do this, we substitute [MATH: x = -6] into the function definition and then simplify:\n[MATH: h(x)|= (x + 6)/(6); h(\u2212 6)|= (\u2212 6 + 6)/(6); = (0)/(6); = 0]\n\nFinally, we calculate [MATH: h(6) - h(-6)] as follows:\n[MATH: h(6) \u2212 h(\u2212 6)|= 2 \u2212 0; = 2]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nThe function [MATH: g] is defined by\n[MATH: g(x) = (x \u2212 4)/(2).]\nWhat is the value of [MATH: g(10) \u2212 g(6)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 2]\nb. [MATH: 4]\nc. [MATH: (3)/(2)]\nd. [MATH: (7)/(2)]\ne. [MATH: 1]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nThe function [MATH: h] is defined by\n[MATH: h(x) = (x + 6)/(6).]\nWhat is the value of [MATH: h(6) \u2212 h(\u2212 6)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 1]\nb. [MATH: 2]\nc. [MATH: 3]\nd. [MATH: 6]\ne. [MATH: 0]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Example: Determining a Linear Combination of Outputs\n\nExample Prompt:\nIf [MATH: p(x) = x - 1] and [MATH: q(x) = 3x,] what is the value of [MATH: 4p(2) - q(2)?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we calculate [MATH: p(2).] To do this, we substitute [MATH: x = 2] into the function definition [MATH: p(x)] and then simplify:\n[MATH: p(x)|= x \u2212 1; p(2)|= 2 \u2212 1; = 1]\n\nNext, we calculate [MATH: q(2).] To do this, we substitute [MATH: x = 2] into the function definition [MATH: q(x)] and then simplify:\n[MATH: q(x)|= 3x; q(2)|= 3(2); = 6]\n\nNow, we calculate [MATH: 4p(2) - q(2)] as follows:\n[MATH: 4p(2) \u2212 q(2)|= 4(1) \u2212 6; = 4 \u2212 6; = \u2212 2]\n\n---\n\nItem 12 \u2014 Question 7\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: p(x) = x \u2212 4] and [MATH: q(x) = 2x,] what is the value of [MATH: 2p(5) \u2212 q(5)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 8]\nb. [MATH: 4]\nc. [MATH: 0]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 8]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 4]\n\n---\n\nItem 13 \u2014 Question 8\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: p(x) = x \u2212 1] and [MATH: q(x) = 3x,] what is the value of [MATH: 4p(2) \u2212 q(2)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 2]\nb. [MATH: 0]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 4]\nd. [MATH: 4]\ne. [MATH: 2]"
